# Ticket 01 Scenario
## Scenario
A customer complains that a text file "report.txt" they created won't let them read or edit it.

## Context
The directory and file was made by me but was modified and edited to create a scenario or possibility where a customer happens to run an issue where their file can't be accessed.

## Objective
- Investigate file permissions
- Identify permissions of owner, group, and others
- Determine why the file can't be accessed
- Correct the permission issue

## Finding the file
Using ls -l, I searched and displayed the directories that were within the terminal. I then used cd Troubleshootinglab to change directories into the 'Troubleshootinglab' directory and then used ls to display all the files in the directory and found the 'report.txt' file.


## Access denied
After trying to display or read the text within report.txt using cat, the terminal states that the permission for reading this file was denied.

## Checking file permissions
Using ls -l, I checked the permission of report.txt and found that the file gave no permission to access, read, or edit the file for neither the owner, group, or other users.

## Changing permissions
To change and fix the permissions, I used chmod 644 report.txt to give the owner permission to read and edit the file while group and other users will only have access to read the files. Using ls -l again, I used this command line to verify that the owner, group, and other users have the correct permissions for the file.
